# old-vs-new (ovs-rtlpg tests/oldnew, 83efa85, 17 scenarios) for feat/sched
# with E1 (its review fixes too) and E3 merged, against fork main b635486: e1-oldnew.expect's lines
# (D1, D3's U4, E1) and e3-oldnew.expect's (the flash job's upload, slower
# and windowed), each once.
stp        002 cli stp status        # D1: STP that much sooner, tx counts +1, ages 40/0 for 39/1
stp        005 web GET /stp.json     # D1: tcs 0x16 for 0x15
stp        006 web GET /stpcnt.json  # D1: the BPDU counters, one more
upload     reg 06f4                  # D1: SEC_COUNTER, the update's reset the other side of a second (per build)
stp_upload reg 06f4                  # the same as upload's
*          reg 06f4                  # E1 (8x): SEC_COUNTER one more at the end: the boot ~162 ms sooner crosses a second
vlan       frames * tcp/80           # U4: the /cmd's reply on a later poll, not with the request's ACK (28 -> 29)
config     frames * tcp/80           # U4 +1 (D3) and E3 +1: the config save's 200 on the poll after the flash job (32 -> 34); SWGT024 under E1 32 -> 25: the old's FIN came after the bench's own, unacknowledged: 8 retransmits and a RST
web        010 web GET /information.json  # E1 (8x): its uptime one second more, the same second
config     frames * rldp             # E1 (8x): one RLDP probe more in the window, the firmware ~162 ms ahead
config     frames * stp              # E1 (8x): one BPDU more, the same
loop       frames * rldp             # E1 + E3 (8x): one RLDP probe more in the window (98 -> 99 on the looped ports), the firmware ahead as config's; D1 and D2 had the same (d1/d2-oldnew.expect), E1 and E3 alone not
lacp_l2    004 console               # E1: the LAG no longer flaps during l2: the old's LACP timed out in its 3.86 s dump (4 port_lag_members_set lines)
lacp_l2    040 cli lacp show         # E1: rx 0x7e for 0x80 on the LAG ports: 2 LACPDUs fewer, below
lacp_l2    041 lacp partner          # E1: in/out 129/132 for 131/134, the same
lacp_l2    frames * lacp             # E1: 129 for 131: gaps a steady 1.01-1.03 s; the old's 3.86 s gap ended in a catch-up burst (3 ms apart)
upload     frames * tcp/80           # E3: the stage's window: window updates once the job has written it (168 -> ~272)
stp_upload frames * tcp/80           # E3: the same
upload     003 console               # E3: the upload takes ~1 s longer, so the boot after it is split at another point between this
upload     003 boot                  #     result and the next (their text, taken together, is the same)
stp_upload 004 console               # E3: one '.' per segment after the first, as before; a client keeping to the window sends more, smaller ones
stp_upload 004 boot                  # E3: the boot after the longer upload split at another point, as upload's
stp_upload frames * stp              # E3: the upload ~1 s longer: one hello more in the scenario
